  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's profile carries fraud_flags = 1. Under POL-GEN-22, where either party's profile carries a fraud flag of one or more, the confidence required for an AI ruling is 0.95 whatever the dispute value, so the sub-10.00 SGD 'final at any confidence' default cannot apply here; POL-NS-26 makes the finality of a no-show ruling expressly subject to that same 0.95 bar. The confidence this case must clear is therefore 0.95, not the ordinary no-show threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-05066"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.fraud_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The half of the POL-NS-23 contact obligation that requires the driver to have messaged the rider rests on the chat log, and that artifact is IMPAIRED: both driver messages were delivered but never read (read_at is null on MSG-05066-001 and MSG-05066-002), giving issue code UNREAD_MESSAGE and weight_multiplier 0.85. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the judge's confidence must not exceed the lowest weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact, so confidence on whether the contact obligation was met is capped at 0.85. I disclose the impairment rather than present this evidence as clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05066"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-CHAT-05066].admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The 0.85 cap on the contact evidence sits below the 0.95 the driver's fraud flag requires, so an AI ruling upholding the 5.00 SGD fee cannot be reached at the confidence POL-GEN-22 demands. The case must therefore go to human review under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26; an escalated fee is held rather than collected, which leaves the rider not carrying the disputed charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-05066", "EV-CHAT-05066", "EV-FARE-05066"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account — 'I never got any message or call' — is corroborated rather than contradicted by the record: both message rows sit unread (read_at null) and the single in-app call rang 20 seconds and was not answered. Whether the driver's contact actually reached the rider is a fact POL-NS-23's obligation turns on, and on an impaired chat log POL-GEN-26 says that fact is not to be resolved by inference from the record but is the open question for escalation. The doubt here is real, not manufactured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05066", "EV-TRIP-05066"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-CHAT-05066].payload.messages.read_at",
      "asserted_weight": 0.85
    },
    {
      "text": "The payments ledger shows the rider is presently out of pocket: total_charged of 5.00 SGD, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. Under POL-GEN-03 an outcome only benefits the rider if it leaves the rider not carrying that charge, and an escalated fee is held rather than collected; a ruling that lets the fee stand as charged leaves the rider carrying it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05066"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

