    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "The 5.00 SGD no-show fee is held for now — it is neither collected nor refunded — and a human reviewer will decide. Here is why, for both sides.\n\nWhat is established. The driver did reach the pickup: the trip record's auto-arrival at 2026-09-11T20:46:45+08:00 is corroborated by the GPS trace (nearest fix 2.64 m from the pickup point, reported accuracy 4 m, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius), each at full weight (POL-NS-21). This was an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, so the 300-second free wait ran from arrival, 20:46:45 to 20:51:45. The driver cancelled at 20:53:00 — 75 seconds after the wait expired, with the platform's wait-timer-expired event at 20:51:50 — so the cancellation was not premature. The payments ledger shows exactly 5.00 SGD charged (EV-FARE-05066), matching the policy fee.\n\nWhy no AI money ruling can issue here. For the fee to stand, POL-NS-23 requires the driver to have messaged the rider AND called the rider before cancelling. The call is properly carried by the trip record at weight 1.0. The message, however, rests on the chat log EV-CHAT-05066, which is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue code UNREAD_MESSAGE — both messages were delivered but never read. The driver's argument that the trip record independently carries the sending at weight 1.0 does not hold: the trip record's message data (message_count, the message list, complete, obligation_met) is taken from that same chat log, so it is the same carrier, not a second, independent one (POL-GEN-02). Remove the chat log and nothing independent shows the driver's messages at all. The evidence carrying this part of the case is therefore capped at 0.85.\n\nThe required confidence. The driver's profile carries fraud_flags = 1, so POL-GEN-22 — and POL-NS-26, which makes a no-show ruling subject to that bar — require confidence of 0.95. The cap of 0.85 is below 0.95, so no AI ruling, whether upholding the 5.00 SGD fee or refunding it, can be issued.\n\nOn the rider's side: the suggestion that the driver 'does this to collect fees' is a pattern allegation about other trips with nothing behind it; profiles may not be used to decide what happened on this trip (POL-GEN-01). The rider's account that no message or call reached them is consistent with the unread messages, but POL-NS-23 turns on what the driver did, and on that point the record is impaired rather than clear.\n\nThe open question for the reviewer is whether the driver's messages actually reached the rider, given the impaired chat log and the confidence the fraud flag requires (POL-GEN-26). Figures used: fee charged 5.00 SGD (EV-FARE-05066); chat log weight 0.85, issue UNREAD_MESSAGE (EV-CHAT-05066); required confidence 0.95 (POL-GEN-22). No refund and no driver compensation is ordered; the 5.00 SGD stays held."
