    "explanation": "To both parties: this case cannot be decided by the AI, and it goes to a human reviewer. The 5.00 SGD cancellation fee is held — not collected from the rider and not paid to the driver — until that review is done.\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS. The driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-05066, complete, weight 1.0) puts him 2.64 m from the pickup point at 20:46:52 with a reported accuracy of 4 m, so the auto-arrival event at 20:46:45 is corroborated well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (POL-NS-21). This was an on-demand trip with no scheduled time, so the 300 s free wait ran from arrival: 20:46:45 + 300 s = 20:51:45. The driver cancelled at 20:53:00, 75 s after the wait expired, and the fare ledger (EV-FARE-05066, complete, weight 1.0) shows exactly the 5.00 SGD fee POL-NS-22 fixes. On arrival and the free wait, the driver's account is made out.\n\nTHE CONTACT OBLIGATION AND THE CONFIDENCE CAP. POL-NS-23 requires the driver to have sent at least one in-app message AND placed at least one in-app call before cancelling. The call is carried by the trip record (EV-TRIP-05066, weight 1.0): one in-app call placed 20:49:30, unanswered, 20 s. The two messages (20:47:00 and 20:50:20) are carried by the chat log EV-CHAT-05066, which is IMPAIRED at weight 0.85 with issue code UNREAD_MESSAGE — both messages were delivered but never opened (read_at is null on MSG-05066-001 and MSG-05066-002). The driver argued the trip record independently carries the messaging at weight 1.0. That does not hold: the trip record's message count and its 'obligation_met' flag are both derived from EV-CHAT-05066, so it is the same measurement in a second artifact, not an independent carrier (POL-GEN-02). The confidence on the deciding fact is therefore capped at 0.85 — the lowest weight among the artifacts carrying it.\n\nWHY THAT IS BELOW THE BAR. The driver's profile (EV-DPROF-05066) carries fraud_flags 1. Under POL-GEN-22, and POL-NS-26 for no-shows, that raises the confidence an AI ruling needs to 0.95 whatever the dispute value. The 0.85 cap is below 0.95, so no AI ruling — for the fee or against it — can issue on this trip, and POL-GEN-26 points the same way (it names 'whether the driver messaged and called before cancelling' as a fact whose carrying evidence, if impaired, escalates). The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-05066-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no fact; traffic is in any event irrelevant to the free-wait test, so it is not part of the reason.\n\nTHE CLAIMS. Driver: the arrival claim and the free-wait claim are accepted; the fraud-flag claim is accepted — it is a confidence dial and raises the bar to 0.95, it does not decide the trip; the POL-NS-24 and unsupported-pattern-allegation claims are accepted (POL-NS-24's refund branch and its goodwill credit are not engaged, since the driver did arrive and did attempt contact); the claim that the trip record independently carries the messaging at 1.0 is rejected for the reason above; the claims that the money matches policy and that no escalation is warranted are rejected as to outcome, because the bar cannot be met. Rider: the claim that 0.95 is required is accepted; the claim that the chat log caps confidence on the contact obligation at 0.85 is accepted, and it is what decides this case; the claim that the rider is presently out of pocket 5.00 SGD is accepted as context — escalation holds that sum rather than collecting it.\n\nFOR THE REVIEWER (open question, not a referral): whether the driver's contact actually reached the rider. Both messages were delivered but unread and the single call rang 20 s unanswered. POL-NS-23 turns on sending, not receipt, but that question cannot be settled to 0.95 on an impaired chat log.\n\nNO REFERRALS. The fee charged is exactly 5.00 SGD, so POL-NS-22's other-amount referral does not fire. POL-NS-24's goodwill credit is not engaged. The POL-NS-25 repeat no-show counter (rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d) is not present on the profile and this trip's fee does not stand, so no flag issues."
